    {
      "id": "run-1793231670848",
      "company": "mct",
      "showAbv": "Urinetown",
      "show": "Urinetown",
      "description": "Winner of three Tony Awards, three Outer Critics Circle Awards, two Lucille Lortel Awards and two Obie Awards, and inspired by the works of Bertolt Brecht and Kurt Weill, *Urinetown* is a musical satire of the legal system, capitalism, social irresponsibility, populism, environmental collapse, privatization of natural resources, bureaucracy, municipal politics, and musical theater itself. Set in a Gotham-like city, a terrible water shortage, caused by a 20-year drought, has led to a government-enforced ban on private toilets. The citizens must use public amenities, regulated by a single malevolent company that profits by charging admission for one of humanity's most basic needs. Amid the people, a hero decides that he's had enough and plans a revolution to lead them all to freedom!\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Mark Hollmann\nBook and Lyric by Greg Kotis\nDirected by Daria E. Troxell",
      "genre": [
        "Musical"
      ],
